        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Phantom5613\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantom5613/48/1906_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Phantom5613:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Boy, this sure is a fun card game, huh?<br>(Nervously trying to change the subject…)</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Were we still in the original thread, maybe that'd be a reasonable thing to do.&nbsp; But the whole point of &gt;G splitting this thread off, as opposed to my deleting the off-topic posts, would appear to be that they consider me entitled to my opinion, and just wanted to get it out of the place where it was off-topic.&nbsp; I'm a big believer in having conversations moved to more appropriate fora (as long as everyone's links take them there so they don't lose track of their communications).&nbsp; So if people want to talk about \"suspension of disbelief and comic book storylines\", this is a place set aside for doing that, and if they don't want to, then the thread can fall dormant until someone does.&nbsp; If you wish to discuss a different subject, there is doubtlessly a different thread where you can most effectively do so.</p>",
