        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Envisioner\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Envisioner:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<div><b>Phantom5613 wrote:</b><br>\n<blockquote>Boy, this sure is a fun card game, huh?(Nervously trying to change the subject...)\n</blockquote>\n</div>\n<p>Were we still in the original thread, maybe that’d be a reasonable thing to do.  But the whole point of &gt;G splitting this thread off, as opposed to my deleting the off-topic posts, would appear to be that they consider me entitled to my opinion, and just wanted to get it out of the place where it was off-topic.  I’m a big believer in having conversations moved to more appropriate fora (as long as everyone’s links take them there so they don’t lose track of their communications).  So if people want to talk about “suspension of disbelief and comic book storylines”, this is a place set aside for doing that, and if they don’t want to, then the thread can fall dormant until someone does.  If you wish to discuss a different subject, there is doubtlessly a different thread where you can most effectively do so.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>You kind of already steered it off topic with this ‘society lesson’ you’re giving us, though. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/confused.png?v=12\" title=\":confused:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":confused:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>",
